(A fixed-layout document is drawn, not laid out: the page arrives with its) Tj T*
(own fonts, its own spacing and its own illustrations already composed, and) Tj T*
(the reader's job is to put those pixels on the screen unchanged.) Tj T*
T*
(That is the whole contract, and it is why this path renders through a) Tj T*
(canvas instead of extracting text. Anything the reader does to a PDF page) Tj T*
(has to happen around the bitmap, never to it.) Tj T*
T*
(Which makes the cost of a page turn a rendering cost, and rendering is) Tj T*
(slow enough to see: a page like this one takes tens of milliseconds, and a) Tj T*
(page dense with vector work takes a good deal more. Whatever the reader is) Tj T*
(looking at during that time is what they will remember about the turn.) Tj T*
T*
(Hence the double buffer. The page already on screen stays there until its) Tj T*
(replacement exists, and the swap between them happens inside a single) Tj T*
(task so the browser never paints the gap.) Tj T*
ET
